+
+# Generate m17 L17 b04 written plan scene asset
+
+## Goal
+
+Generate one course scene PNG at `course-assets/scenes/module-17/m17_L17_b04_written-plan.png`.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Use the attached BMH course doodle references and locked flat sticker-sheet style.
+- Use gpt-image-2 through the built-in image generation workflow.
+- Create one 1600 x 900 PNG.
+- Show a neat stack of official blank documents sitting in a cream folder.
+- Imply one offer-letter-shaped page, one comp-plan-shaped page, and one role-sheet-shaped page only by form factor.
+- Allow a few abstract unreadable horizontal line strokes and empty boxes only.
+- Leave clean bottom-center cornflower blue space for code-rendered sticker text.
+- Use thick wobbly black outlines, rounded simple shapes, flat fills only, and the locked palette: cornflower blue, sunflower yellow, tangerine orange, pale cream, white, and black.
+- Avoid people, faces, money, text, words, letters, numbers, symbols, dollar signs, labels, tables, ambient doodles, motion marks, icons, random props, gradients, texture, shadows, lighting, and perspective depth.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Confirm the file exists at the requested path.
+- Confirm the file is a PNG at 1600 x 900.
+- Confirm palette flattening leaves only locked course colors.
+- Visually inspect for a blank document stack in a cream folder, bottom-center blue space, no people, no money, no readable paperwork, no text, no symbols, and no decorative clutter.

codex
The prompt is going to be strict because the failure modes are predictable: generated models tend to add labels, dollar marks, forms, signatures, and decorative doodles. I’m explicitly banning those and asking for form factor only.
codex
The generated composition is usable, but it violates the flat-fill requirement with soft gradients. I’m going to flatten it locally to the locked palette before saving, then inspect the final PNG.
